      "mergeID": "64f89834e15f5a66d6355d43",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Not possible to scale some avatars in the beta. They are stuck in what size they were in before loading in. Resetting the avatar doesn't set it to it's original size. Scaling shows them changing size in the preview mirror. But snaps back to the size you started as.\n\nPeople that aren't on the beta are able to scale their avatar. But it stays the original size on the beta side. Players not in the beta see them scaling as they should. As described in this one: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1342-avatar-scale If you hide their avatar they go to a properly sized robot.\n\nHere is two avatars I've found the problem on.\n\navtr_b2402986-60a3-4c1c-a27c-7fa8dc7b4d1a\n\navtr_01a08e25-6531-4e44-a5e5-6297ba0fe8cf\n\nHere is a video showing the problem. Notice the avatar on the left that is half way into the ground. That one should be more like 40cm in size.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/57eOGvcW1X8\n\nhttps://gist.github.com/Tummy-git/ba3bf55fb1cd8c50ae12dc114954cdc7",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1344] avatar scaling not working.",
